WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.451 --> 00:00:04.207
Unit twelve. Introduction to the Cloud!

2
00:00:05.145 --> 00:00:10.120
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:13.215
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.265 --> 00:00:17.623
Today we learn about Introduction to the Cloud. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.807
Cloud. Say it with me. Cloud!

6
00:00:26.323 --> 00:00:30.618
Store online. Say it with me. Store online!

7
00:00:34.172 --> 00:00:39.138
Access anywhere. Say it with me. Access anywhere!

8
00:00:42.632 --> 00:00:47.531
Internet connection. Say it with me. Internet connection!

9
00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:54.579
Backup. Say it with me. Backup!

10
00:00:58.094 --> 00:01:01.794
Sync. Say it with me. Sync!

11
00:01:05.232 --> 00:01:09.265
Upload. Say it with me. Upload!

12
00:01:12.778 --> 00:01:16.893
Server. Say it with me. Server!

13
00:01:20.398 --> 00:01:30.366
The cloud lets me store files online instead of only on my device. I can access them anywhere with an internet connection, and they sync as a backup.

14
00:01:30.416 --> 00:01:33.712
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:34.449 --> 00:01:40.002
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.052 --> 00:01:41.664
Access anywhere!

17
00:01:42.646 --> 00:01:47.967
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.017 --> 00:01:49.167
Upload!

19
00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:59.507
Did you know? 'The cloud' isn't actually in the sky — it refers to powerful computers called servers stored in buildings around the world!

20
00:01:59.557 --> 00:02:01.844
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:02.676 --> 00:02:13.613
Think and answer. What is one benefit of storing a file in the cloud instead of only on one device?

22
00:02:13.663 --> 00:02:14.818
Great answer!

23
00:02:15.763 --> 00:02:21.097
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:21.147 --> 00:02:24.249
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

